{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06/result.md'","aggregated_output":"# P06 context, chronology, and resolution result\n\nPASS: 27 P06 tests, 11 P03 regression tests, and 21 P04 regression tests executed. The conformance file records every test outcome, independent criterion probe, source hash, inventory comparison, command, and manifest.\n\nRepair replaced metadata-only harmonisation with derived identity observations, enforced reference/date/domain admission, bound resolution to constituent values, and connected selected evidence to period derivation and debt arithmetic. The runtime preserves earlier result copies and rejects conflicting revisions. Original evidence selection retains eligible lineage roots when later revisions exist; latest selection alone removes superseded roots. Malformed joint laws, historical constraints, and election treatment lists now receive stable category-specific rejection codes.\n\nThe implementation supplies explicit context mappings, finite partition enumeration, supersession-DAG evidence selection, date-only next-local-midnight handling, revision-compatible YTD subtraction, six category-specific uncertainty admission, information-view guards, and query-signature-bound fixed-rate unhedged bullet-debt resolution. Exact Fraction arithmetic is used throughout the supported scalar path. An approximation is accepted only with a fixed-rate scope, declared tolerance, and a triangle-inequality error certificate.\n\nThe tests independently verify 260 minus revised H1 110 equals H2 150 and reject subtraction using incompatible original H1 120. They reject parent/group, basis, measurement, currency, calendar, gross/net, overlap, omission, dangling/cyclic revision, future-information, unsupported treatment, unsupported scenario, stale-query, maturity-crossing, and missing-approximation-evidence cases. Historical byte availability marked unknown remains unresolved and is excluded from the integrated historical computation. Tests also mutate the selected H1 amount from 110 to 100: derived H2 changes from 150 to 160, and the synthetic debt interest changes from 7.5 to 8, while the preserved earlier result remains 150.\n\nSpecified behaviour is recorded in the versioned profile. Implemented operations and independently tested invariants are bounded to those operations; synthetic permissions and evidence references do not establish accounting eligibility or source truth. Identity harmonisation, finite scalar historical domains, a hold policy, and exact integer-period DCF are supported; broader transformations/policies are explicitly unsupported.\n\n| Decision | Primary criterion | Veto status | Main uncertainty | Next justified action | Not concluded |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| PASS for bounded engineering conformance | Independent P06 probes and focused/regression suites | tests=True; protection=True; stable=True; failed_observations=[] | finite synthetic cases and unannotated source availability | independent result review if PASS; repair if FAIL | professional accounting validity, empirical forecast validity, human acceptance, or wider MC01–MC35/G1–G18 closure |\n\nEngineering correctness, numerical validity, and interpretation remain separate. The exact outputs establish only the declared bounded operations. The strongest alternative explanation is a shared interpretation error in the synthetic fixtures; independent set and arithmetic probes reduce that risk but do not replace source or professional review. The weakest evidence is breadth: mappings, uncertainty, and grouping are finite bounded cases.\n\nResiduals: general measurement conversion, consolidation, arbitrary calendars, continuous or nonlinear uncertainty, empirical approximation validation, historical retained-byte availability, accounting validity, forecast validity, and human acceptance remain open. This phase does not rank stochastic candidates or establish a production default.\n\nActual command: `CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=-1 python3 -B scripts/check_accounting_p06.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P06 --approved-plan data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/approved-plan.json --execution-inventory data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T233421-cea9e631/P06/execution-1/pre-edit-files.json`. Python 3.11.15, CPU only with accelerator devices intentionally hidden. Wall time: 4.462543 seconds. Git provenance is unavailable; content hashes and supervisor inventories are retained in conformance.json.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
